115:node scripts/gen_job_schema.mjs --check           # exit 1 when a schema or its ledger is stale
119:Their ledgers are `JOB_VERSIONS.json`, `RUNNER_FILE_VERSIONS.json`, `JOB_RECEIPT_VERSIONS.json` and `JOB_STATUS_VERSIONS.json`, entries `{ "schema_version", "schemaSha256", "note" }`, newest last, under the same rule as the run-result ledger with `JOB_RECORD_VERSION`, `RUNNER_FILE_VERSION`, `JOB_RECEIPT_SCHEMA_VERSION` and `JOB_STATUS_SCHEMA_VERSION`. The job record and the runner's files carry their version in the member `version`; the ledgers key it as `schema_version` like every other ledger here. Their version rule is the policy document's: the readers (`parseJobRecord`, `parseRunnerRequest` and the rest) refuse any other version and any key they do not know, so every added, removed or changed member bumps the version. A receipt and a status document are reports for other tools, so an added optional member keeps their version. `cli/test/runner_store.test.ts` and `cli/test/job_receipt_schema.test.ts` run the comparisons and validate sample documents.

